'Who did you pass on the road?' the King went on, holding out his hand to t=
he Messenger for some more hay.
'Nobody,' said the Messenger.
'Quite right,' said the King: 'this young lady saw him too. So of course No=
body walks slower than you.'
'I do my best,' the Messenger said in a sulky tone. 'I'm sure nobody walks =
much faster than I do!'
'He can't do that,' said the King, 'or else he'd have been here first.


